Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.307 --> 00:00:08.620
How a Revolver Works: 
Colt Python

00:00:12.266 --> 00:00:17.126
A colt python is loaded by first&nbsp;
pulling the 'cylinder latch' to the rear.

00:00:18.446 --> 00:00:22.586
This unlocks the cylinder by means&nbsp;
of the spring-loaded 'latch pin'.

00:00:25.646 --> 00:00:29.726
The 'crane' is now able to swivel&nbsp;
the cylinder out of the frame.

00:00:31.466 --> 00:00:34.708
Cartridges are then loaded
into all six&nbsp;chambers.

00:00:35.878 --> 00:00:38.545
The cylinder is then pushed back&nbsp;into the frame 

00:00:38.545 --> 00:00:42.786
and then rotated to ensure&nbsp;
the 'bolt' has locked it into position.

00:00:44.846 --> 00:00:49.766
Many revolvers feature both
double-action and single-action operation.

00:00:50.546 --> 00:00:54.586
In double-action operation,
the 'trigger' is pulled&nbsp;until it cocks

00:00:54.586 --> 00:00:57.048
and releases the hammer to fire.

00:00:57.506 --> 00:00:59.337
In single-action operation,

00:00:59.337 --> 00:01:03.713
the 'hammer' is drawn&nbsp;back to the cocked position,
and held by the sear.

00:01:04.706 --> 00:01:08.186
Squeezing the trigger releases the hammer to fire.

00:01:12.506 --> 00:01:18.025
As the trigger is pulled, the trigger pushes up on&nbsp;
the 'hammer strut', cocking the hammer.

00:01:18.793 --> 00:01:22.013
As the hammer&nbsp;rotates,
the 'main spring' is compressed

00:01:22.013 --> 00:01:25.083
by means of&nbsp;the 'hammer stirrup'
and the 'rebound lever'

00:01:25.083 --> 00:01:27.252
which is&nbsp;pushed up by the trigger.

00:01:27.866 --> 00:01:32.308
As the hammer reaches&nbsp;its cocked position,
it slips off the trigger.

00:01:34.166 --> 00:01:40.106
Simultaneously the trigger pushes down on the&nbsp;'bolt',
dropping it out of the cylinder pocket.

00:01:42.866 --> 00:01:48.746
The 'hand' engages the ratchet of the cylinder&nbsp;ejector,
indexing it to the next chamber.

00:01:49.586 --> 00:01:55.706
Just as the hammer is released, the bolt drops into&nbsp;
the next pocket, locking the cylinders rotation.

00:01:56.606 --> 00:02:01.875
At the same time, the trigger raises the&nbsp;
'transfer bar' up behind the firing pin.

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:05.786
As the hammer is released, 
it strikes&nbsp;the transfer bar, 

00:02:05.786 --> 00:02:12.124
transferring its&nbsp;energy to the firing pin, 
which travels forward,&nbsp;impacting the 'cartridge primer'.

00:02:13.282 --> 00:02:19.586
This detonates&nbsp;the priming compound and ignites
the powder&nbsp;charge, propelling the bullet down the barrel.

00:02:22.286 --> 00:02:26.160
With the rebound lever under constant&nbsp;
tension from the main spring,

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.624
its tension&nbsp;is transferred to the trigger.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:32.632
Releasing the trigger,
pivots the&nbsp;'hammer strut' out of the way, 

00:02:32.632 --> 00:02:35.597
allowing&nbsp;it to return to its forward position.

00:02:37.346 --> 00:02:41.160
During single-action operation,
the&nbsp;hammer is pulled back,

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.076
driving movement&nbsp;of the trigger. 

00:02:43.408 --> 00:02:47.219
At its peak, the trigger&nbsp;
rests on the sear surface of the hammer.

00:02:47.786 --> 00:02:53.079
Pulling the trigger, releases it from the hammer sear, 
allowing it to strike the transfer bar.

00:02:53.632 --> 00:02:57.425
Releasing the trigger, 
again&nbsp;resets its forward position.

00:03:15.746 --> 00:03:19.625
To eject the empty shell cases, 
the&nbsp;cylinder latch is pulled,

00:03:19.625 --> 00:03:22.037
allowing the&nbsp;cylinder to swivel out of the frame.

00:03:22.712 --> 00:03:27.202
Holding the revolver in a vertical&nbsp;orientation 
and pushing the 'ejector rod',

00:03:27.202 --> 00:03:29.861
forces the cases out of the cylinder.

